WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.116 --> 00:00:11.058
Jimmy's family was on their way to a beach vacation.

2
00:00:13.659 --> 00:00:18.222
As they drove along, his parents and twin brother Jason were talking excitedly.

3
00:00:18.242 --> 00:00:24.185
"I'm going to walk on the beach every morning," Mom said.

4
00:00:24.205 --> 00:00:28.428
"I'm going fishing," Dad said.

5
00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:32.353
"Can we go to the amusement park?"

6
00:00:32.693 --> 00:00:33.473
Jason asked.

7
00:00:33.493 --> 00:00:38.115
"There's a new roller coaster—Motion Monster."

8
00:00:40.676 --> 00:00:41.817
Jimmy stayed quiet.

9
00:00:44.238 --> 00:00:45.298
"What's wrong, Jimmy?"

10
00:00:45.619 --> 00:00:46.379
Mom asked.

11
00:00:51.181 --> 00:00:51.901
He shrugged.

12
00:00:51.921 --> 00:00:56.623
"Nothing." "I know what's wrong!"

13
00:00:57.003 --> 00:00:57.824
Jason grinned.

14
00:01:00.268 --> 00:01:01.889
"This is a long car ride.

15
00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:06.171
He's worried he's going to throw up!"

16
00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:12.253
"I brought some stuff, in case you do feel carsick."

17
00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:13.854
Mom held up a bag.

18
00:01:13.874 --> 00:01:20.877
"I've got peppermint gum, ginger candy, wristbands, and even some medicine.

19
00:01:22.258 --> 00:01:23.898
One of these treatments might help."

20
00:01:25.399 --> 00:01:26.299
Jimmy sighed.

21
00:01:29.192 --> 00:01:31.294
"Why do I get carsick anyway?"

22
00:01:31.314 --> 00:01:36.378
"It's called motion sickness," Mom said.

23
00:01:36.398 --> 00:01:41.122
"It comes from your ears and your eyes having a disagreement."

24
00:01:43.484 --> 00:01:46.807
"Kind of like Jimmy looked at Jason.

25
00:01:46.827 --> 00:01:49.309
"Twins disagreeing?"

26
00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:52.632
"Not exactly," Mom said.

27
00:01:52.652 --> 00:01:59.165
"Motion sickness occurs when one sense detects motion, but another one does not.

28
00:02:00.806 --> 00:02:04.968
For example, if you're reading in the car, your eyes think you're staying still.

29
00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:10.971
Meanwhile your ears detect motion, and the two senses clash."

30
00:02:10.991 --> 00:02:15.574
"So your brain gets different messages," Dad added.

31
00:02:15.594 --> 00:02:18.596
"And you start to sweat or feel sick to your stomach."

32
00:02:24.139 --> 00:02:26.460
never get carsick," Jason bragged.

33
00:02:28.184 --> 00:02:33.408
"Doctors aren't sure why some people get motion sickness and others do not," Mom said.

34
00:02:33.428 --> 00:02:37.831
"But it's very common, especially among kids."

35
00:02:37.851 --> 00:02:42.674
"Grandma gets motion sickness on airplanes," Dad said.

36
00:02:46.317 --> 00:02:48.318
friend Shin gets seasick on boats.

37
00:02:49.659 --> 00:02:54.282
He eats ginger before he goes sailing—that's what Chinese fishermen have done for centuries.

38
00:02:55.943 --> 00:02:56.944
It calms your stomach.

39
00:02:57.416 --> 00:03:00.058
Another trick is to stare at the horizon when you're seasick."

40
00:03:04.741 --> 00:03:07.703
Jimmy could see that their car was approaching a curvy road.

41
00:03:07.723 --> 00:03:11.966
"Here." Mom handed him the gum.

42
00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.991
doctor said peppermint is good for stomachaches.

43
00:03:20.493 --> 00:03:22.214
Roll down your window for fresh air.

44
00:03:23.535 --> 00:03:25.096
Don't read or look at a screen."

45
00:03:27.124 --> 00:03:28.685
Jimmy followed his mom's advice.

46
00:03:30.126 --> 00:03:33.568
As the car drove along the road, he chewed gum and closed his eyes.

47
00:03:33.588 --> 00:03:36.529
"How's it going?"

48
00:03:36.829 --> 00:03:37.470
Mom asked.

49
00:03:40.631 --> 00:03:41.832
He took a deep breath.

50
00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:45.614
"Good! I feel fine!"

51
00:03:47.535 --> 00:03:49.296
The week at the beach flew by.

52
00:03:53.698 --> 00:03:56.360
One cloudy day the family went to the amusement park.

53
00:03:58.868 --> 00:04:00.289
"Whoa, check it out!"

54
00:04:01.569 --> 00:04:03.410
Jason pointed to Motion Monster.

55
00:04:04.671 --> 00:04:08.773
It was an enormous roller coaster with steep hills and huge loops.

56
00:04:08.793 --> 00:04:10.694
"Let's go!"

57
00:04:10.714 --> 00:04:19.177
The twins raced over to the ride and hopped into the first car.

58
00:04:21.599 --> 00:04:24.360
Minutes later they began going up the first slope.

59
00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.341
"Ahh!" Jason screamed as they flew downward.

60
00:04:34.121 --> 00:04:35.382
Jimmy threw his arms up.

61
00:04:35.402 --> 00:04:38.403
"Whee! This is awesome!"

62
00:04:44.385 --> 00:04:48.306
But when he looked over at his twin, he saw Jason clutching his stomach.

63
00:04:50.027 --> 00:04:50.927
"What's wrong?"

64
00:04:51.407 --> 00:04:52.087
Jimmy asked.

65
00:04:52.787 --> 00:04:54.108
But he already knew the answer.

66
00:04:59.597 --> 00:05:01.533
Jason had motion sickness!
